{"key":"enterprise/T1546.005","id":"T1546.005","name":"Trap","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1546","tactics":["persistence","privilege-escalation"],"platforms":["macOS","Linux"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may establish persistence by executing malicious content triggered by an interrupt signal. The trap command allows programs and shells to specify commands that will be executed upon receiving interrupt signals. A common situation is a script allowing for graceful termination and handling of common keyboard interrupts like ctrl+c and ctrl+d. Adversaries can use this to register code to be executed when the shell encounters specific…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1546/005","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--63220765-d418-44de-8fae-694b3912317d","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:48:51.725Z","source_object_version":"1.1","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0055","name":"File Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0055","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--235b7491-2d2b-4617-9a52-3c0783680f71","page":"telemetry/DC0055/"},{"id":"DC0061","name":"File Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0061","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--84572de3-9583-4c73-aabd-06ea88123dd8","page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0369","name":"Detection Strategy for Event Triggered Execution via Trap (T1546.005)","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0369","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--07fb6847-efcb-426e-9344-bfc9dfcdebd4","relationship_id":"relationship--2bc6f48f-6580-46d3-aefc-666ef4029233"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN1038","name":"Analytic 1038","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0369#AN1038","guidance":"Correlate file modifications in shell startup scripts (e.g., .bashrc, .profile) with embedded `trap` commands and observe if those changes are followed by the unexpected execution of child processes when terminal signals (e.g., SIGINT) are triggered. Use contextual linking with user session activity to detect privilege misuse.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0369"},{"id":"AN1039","name":"Analytic 1039","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0369#AN1039","guidance":"Detect unauthorized `trap` command registrations in shell startup files (e.g., .zprofile, .bash_profile, .zshrc) followed by execution chains during user terminal interaction. Use Unified Logs and EDR telemetry to correlate shell command parsing and process tree anomalies.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0369"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"auditd:SYSCALL","channel":"execve","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN1038","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0369#AN1038","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0061","component":"File Modification","name":"auditd:SYSCALL","channel":"Modification of user shell profile or trap registration via echo/redirection (e.g., echo \"trap 'malicious_cmd' INT\" >> ~/.bashrc)","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN1038","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0369#AN1038","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"component_id":"DC0055","component":"File Access","name":"auditd:SYSCALL","channel":"open","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN1038","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0369#AN1038","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0055/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component"